        "findings": [
          {
            "severity": "major",
            "location": "### 1. Components — \"Parses libraryfolders.vdf to find library paths, then scans steamapps/appmanifest_*.acf for game metadata.\"",
            "problem": "The design relies on values from local files (.vdf, .acf) and the Windows Registry to construct the `install_path`. Since these sources are untrusted, a malicious actor could use `..` or absolute paths to cause path traversal.",
            "fix": "Implement path canonicalization and validate that the resulting `install_path` is a child of a verified library directory."
          },
          {
            "severity": "major",
            "location": "### 1. Components — \"Parses libraryfolders.vdf to find library paths, then scans steamapps/appmanifest_*.acf for game metadata.\"",
            "problem": "The parsing of .vdf and .acf files does not specify resource limits. Maliciously large or complex files could cause a Denial of Service (DoS) via memory exhaustion.",
            "fix": "Enforce strict maximum file size limits and use a parser that handles malformed/deeply nested structures with bounded resource usage."
          }
        ]
      },
